@gopidesupavan you are right, but now I don't understand what you want to achieve with this PR. Because in an issue https://github.com/apache/airflow/issues/41877 I see that the user wants to see the same XCom result on deff and non-deff mode. If you add conversion in trigger side then trigger returns string to `execute_complete` and after that a `return` statement adds this value to XCom. As a result we will still have different values on deff and non-deff mode.

Also, I see that in non-deff mode the result value depends on `messages_callback` function https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/airflow/providers/google/cloud/sensors/pubsub.py#L146C1-L150C1
In this case for us it means that for consistent values we need to use `handle_messages` function for conversion in deff mode either.

```suggestion
    def execute_complete(self, context: Context, event: dict[str, str | list[str]]) -> list[Any]:
```
